  [
   "Browser extension: FERB asked Google Chrome, Brave to install it from the Chrome Web Store. Each installs it at its next start, for all its profiles, and asks you to turn it on in each profile. FERB never restarts a browser or answers its prompts.",
   "  Google Chrome: install requested",
   "    “Person 1” (a@example.test, Default): installed unpacked, enabled, pairing not checked (FERB isn't running)",
   "    “Work” (work@example.test, Profile 1): installed from the Web Store, waiting for you to turn it on",
   "    “Home” (Profile 3): installed from the Web Store, waiting for you to turn it on",
   "    “Work” (other@example.test, Profile 4): removed earlier, so the browser won't add it again: add it from https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/plbfkifcmgkgnlfgikdeaaglgncdhkma",
   "  Brave: install requested (unconfirmed: Brave doesn't document this folder; it loads extensions as Chromium does; if FERB isn't offered after you reopen it, add it from https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/plbfkifcmgkgnlfgikdeaaglgncdhkma)",
   "    “Brave Main” (Default): installed from the Web Store, waiting for you to turn it on",
   "  To pair a profile with FERB turned on: Pair all or Pair in FERB's Settings → Browsers, or `ferb browsers pair --browser <browser> \"<profile>\"`."
